CHUNK [103 bytes]: ", or should we focus on the raw list of tropes per book?*\n\n---\n\n# Final Product Specification Document:"
CHUNK [136 bytes]: " TropeMapper\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n**TropeMapper** is a Digital Humanities platform designed for the longitudinal analysis of fiction"
CHUNK [102 bytes]: " (novels, scripts, and series). It combines structural NLP (BookNLP) with semantic reasoning (LLMs) to"
CHUNK [154 bytes]: " identify tropes, attribute them to specific characters through dialogue and coreference, and maintain consistency across multiple volumes of a series via"
CHUNK [143 bytes]: " user-driven feedback loops.\n\n## 2. Problem Statement\nAnalyzing tropes in long-form fiction is traditionally manual and prone to inconsistency."
CHUNK [118 bytes]: " Existing tools lack the ability to:\n1.  Attribute tropes to specific characters over thousands of pages.\n2.  Maintain"
CHUNK [107 bytes]: " a \"Ground Truth\" of trope definitions across a multi-book series.\n3.  Visualize the evolution of narrative"
CHUNK [106 bytes]: " patterns.\n\n## 3. Ideal User Persona\n*   **The Digital Humanities Scholar:** Quantifying genre shifts over"
CHUNK [128 bytes]: " time.\n*   **The Script/Series Editor:** Ensuring character consistency and trope subversion across multiple episodes or volumes"
CHUNK [87 bytes]: ".\n*   **The Narrative Analyst:** Mapping the \"DNA\" of a specific author’s style.\n\n## "
CHUNK [95 bytes]: "4. Platform & Technical Stack\n*   **Platform:** Desktop Web Application (Next.js/React).\n*   **"
CHUNK [104 bytes]: "Backend:** Python (FastAPI), BookNLP (for structure), OpenAI/Anthropic API (for trope reasoning).\n*   **"
CHUNK [122 bytes]: "Database:** PostgreSQL (Metadata/User data) + PGVector (for semantic trope matching and cross-volume verification).\n\n## 5."
CHUNK [105 bytes]: " Core User Experience (The \"Series\" Flow)\n1.  **Project Creation:** User creates a \"Project Container\" (e"
CHUNK [68 bytes]: ".g., *The Harry Potter Series*).\n2.  **Initial Scan (Book 1):** User"
CHUNK [112 bytes]: " uploads the first volume. The AI performs a \"Deep Scan\" (Background processing for novels).\n3.  **Tuning:** The"
CHUNK [120 bytes]: " user reviews \"Trope Cards,\" upvoting/downvoting detections. The AI builds a **\"Project Profile\"** based on these votes."
CHUNK [71 bytes]: "\n4.  **Cross-Volume Upload (Book 2+):** User uploads the next volume.\n5"
CHUNK [129 bytes]: ".  **Verification:** The AI compares Book 2 against the Project Profile. If it finds a pattern that the user previously rejected,"
CHUNK [130 bytes]: " it flags it in the **Conflict Center** for manual override or confirmation.\n6.  **Comparison:** User views the \"Series Evolution\""
CHUNK [90 bytes]: " dashboard to see how tropes change from Book 1 to Book 2.\n\n## 6. Must-Have Features (MVP)"
CHUNK [116 bytes]: "\n*   **Advanced BookNLP Integration:** Character Coreference, NER (Places/Concepts), and **Quotation Attribution** ("
CHUNK [88 bytes]: "Who said what).\n*   **Dual-Tier Processing:** Real-time for <10k words; Background queue"
CHUNK [114 bytes]: " for novels.\n*   **The Trope Card System:** Links trope definitions to \"Evidence Clusters\" (multiple text snippets"
CHUNK [110 bytes]: ").\n*   **Project-Level Adaptation:** AI adjusts detection sensitivity based on user upvotes/downvotes within a"
CHUNK [121 bytes]: " project.\n*   **Cross-Volume Verification:** A \"Conflict Inbox\" to manage consistency across multiple files in a series.\n"
CHUNK [106 bytes]: "*   **Visualization Suite:** \n    *   **Trope Heatmap:** Narrative density over the manuscript.\n    *   **"
CHUNK [129 bytes]: "Character-Trope Matrix:** Which tropes belong to whom.\n    *   **Series Drift Chart:** How trope usage changes between volumes.\n\n"
CHUNK [114 bytes]: "## 7. Data & Persistence\n*   **User Accounts:** To save \"Project Containers\" and custom sensitivity profiles.\n*   "
CHUNK [91 bytes]: "**Data Persistence:**\n    *   **Raw Text:** Encrypted storage of manuscripts.\n    *   **The"
CHUNK [105 bytes]: " \"Project Profile\":** A JSON-based map of user votes and \"Negative Context\" (rejected tropes).\n    *   **"
CHUNK [145 bytes]: "Annotations:** User-written notes linked to specific entities or trope instances.\n*   **Access Controls:** Projects are private by default; share"
CHUNK [93 bytes]: "able via \"Public Research Link.\"\n\n## 8. Technical Logic: The \"Conflict Engine\"\n*   **Matching"
CHUNK [101 bytes]: ":** Uses semantic embeddings to compare a \"New Instance\" in Book 2 to a \"Rejected Instance\" in Book 1"
CHUNK [93 bytes]: ".\n*   **Thresholding:** If the similarity score is >85%, the AI suppresses the trope but adds"
